/-!
# Continuous mild rows generated by the velocity endpoint

The source-generated velocity Galerkin family already has two properties on
the same actual radius lineage: strong convergence in the whole
`L²_t(ℓ²)` carrier and compactness of every finite continuous observation.
This module consumes both before the time quotient.  For every Fourier row
it generates a continuous representative of the common strong limit and
transports the exact finite unforced equation to the causal heat/Duhamel
identity.

The continuous row, its refining subsequence, and its nonlinear limit are
outputs.  No target path, endpoint value, cutoff, or continuation witness is
accepted by the source-facing theorem.
-/

